  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I am attempting to make a mirror, and part of that involves modifying the projection matrix of the mirror's camera. Unfortunately, this causes culling to get flipped, rendering back-faces instead of front-faces. The normal solution to this if one is using C# is to set GL.invertCulling to True on PreRender and False on PostRender. \n\nObviously, you wouldn't just want to expose GL.invertCulling through a node as that would allow one to invert the culling on the player's camera. Perhaps you could add a node that internally both sets invertCulling to true during prerender and back to false during post render so it can't effect the player's camera.",
